      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.1 descriptive attacks – Characterising or describing women in a derogatory manner. This could include, but not limited to: negative generalisations about women’s abilities, appearance, sexual behaviour, intellect, character, or morals.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Different adjectives are sometimes used to describe the same feature in women and men, reflecting social judgments that treat traits such as ambition as attractive in men but negative in women. Words without explicit gender can still carry strong gender associations and promote stereotypes. Checking whether a descriptive word would also be used for a man can help identify gendered language and guide the choice of a term without gender connotations.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "answer_relevance_card_2ade9986523ba7154e801079__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
