      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks – Expressing strong negative sentiment against women, such as disgust or hatred. This can be through direct description of the speaker’s subjective emotions, baseless accusations, or the use of gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and gender-based insults.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Flaming is an aggressive, hostile, profanity-laced form of online communication characterized by insults, negative affect, and typographic energy such as capital letters and exclamation marks. It involves deliberately swearing or using offensive language to express emotionally charged or contrarian statements, often to elicit a response. Flaming tends to occur in online discussions about controversial political, social, cultural, or religious issues. It can be openly misogynous and is often targeted at women with threats, fantasies of sexual violence, or incitement to sexual violence.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
