        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.3 dehumanising attacks and overt sexual objectification – Derogating women by comparing them to non-human entities such as vermin, disease or refuse, or overtly reducing them to sexual objects.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist hate speech is a form of violence against women and girls that perpetuates and exacerbates gender inequality. It occurs online and offline across schools, families, social circles, public space, work, emails, websites, and social media, and its root causes are linked to persistent unequal power relations between women and men. Combating it requires knowledge and policy action at all levels, including gender equality strategies that treat sexism as a form of hate speech.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
