      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.3 dehumanising attacks and overt sexual objectification – Derogating women by comparing them to non-human entities such as vermin, disease or refuse, or overtly reducing them to sexual objects.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Gendered hate speech targets women because of their gender, reinforces systemic inequalities, makes it difficult for targeted groups to engage online, and can spill over into the physical world, causing violence and death. No dehumanising comparisons to vermin, disease, or refuse and no overt sexual objectification are specified.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
