      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.3 backhanded gendered compliments – Ostensibly complimenting women, but actually belittling or implying their inferiority. This could include, but is not limited to: reduction of women’s value to their attractiveness or sexual desirability, or implication that women are innately frail, helpless or weak.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Spoken or written words based on the idea that people are inferior because of their sex fall within the definition of sexism when their purpose or effect includes violating dignity or rights, causing harm, creating a degrading or offensive environment, restricting autonomy, or reinforcing gender stereotypes. This definition applies in public and private settings, both online and offline.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
