      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.4 condescending explanations or unwelcome advice – Offering unsolicited or patronising advice to women on topics and issues they know more about (known as ‘mansplaining’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Mansplaining involves a man explaining something to a woman in a condescending, patronising, overconfident or oversimplified manner, or assuming that she has no knowledge of the topic. The relevant pattern is an explanatory approach that treats the woman as uninformed rather than recognising her existing knowledge.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
