      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.4 condescending explanations or unwelcome advice – Offering unsolicited or patronising advice to women on topics and issues they know more about (known as ‘mansplaining’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Everyday sexism includes apparently inconsequential or minor sexist behaviour, comments and jokes that are often humiliating. Such acts contribute to a social climate in which women are demeaned, their self-regard is lowered, and their activities and choices are restricted, including at work and in private, public or online spheres. Everyday sexism sits on a continuum with gender stereotypes, gender inequality and violence against women and girls, and sexist behaviour may escalate to or incite overtly offensive and threatening acts.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
