    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID130",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_bbd6606239f0daf35cc076dc__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">A framework to prevent violence against women\n\n1. The problem\n\nViolence and the threat of violence against women (VAW), including those women experiencing multiple and intersecting forms of discrimination. Such violence is a form of discrimination against women which impairs or nullifies the enjoyment by women of human rights and fundamental freedoms. It is also an obstacle to national development and poverty reduction goals. Its health, social and economic impacts extend to children, communities and society as whole.\n\n2. Conditions that need to be addressed to eliminate the problem\n\n1. Individual, relationship, community, organizational and societal/l structures, laws and policies, practices and social norms that:\n(a) Support gender inequality, as manifested in:\n discrimination against women, and their unequal access to power and resources in public and private life;\n harmful constructions of masculinity (e.g. entitled, aggressive, dominant) and femininity (e.g. subordinate, sexualized, objectified);\n stereotyped gender roles; and\n negative male peer associations and weak peer associations among women and girls\n(b) Condone, tolerate, perpetuate and/or positively portray the use of VAW.\n\n2. Exposure to violence in the family, the community, organizations and institutions\n\n3. Other circumstances and contexts that interact or intersect with gender inequality to increase the probability of violence being perpetrated against women (e.g. poverty, alcohol misuse).</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Violence against women is a form of discrimination that impairs women’s enjoyment of human rights and fundamental freedoms. Conditions that must be addressed to eliminate violence include individual, relationship, community, organizational, and societal structures, laws, policies, practices, and social norms that support gender inequality or condone, tolerate, perpetuate, and/or positively portray the use of violence against women. Such norms include discrimination against women and unequal access to power and resources, harmful constructions of masculinity and femininity, stereotyped gender roles, and negative male peer associations and weak peer associations among women and girls.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_bbd6606239f0daf35cc076dc__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
        "QuestionType": "MC",
        "Selector": "SAVR",
        "SubSelector": "TX",
