      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>4.1 supporting mistreatment of individual women – Expressing support for mistreatment of women as individuals. Support can be shown by denying, understating, or seeking to justify such mistreatment.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Violence against women is a form of discrimination that impairs women’s enjoyment of human rights and fundamental freedoms. Conditions that must be addressed to eliminate violence include individual, relationship, community, organizational, and societal structures, laws, policies, practices, and social norms that support gender inequality or condone, tolerate, perpetuate, and/or positively portray the use of violence against women. Such norms include discrimination against women and unequal access to power and resources, harmful constructions of masculinity and femininity, stereotyped gender roles, and negative male peer associations and weak peer associations among women and girls.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
