      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_6a51d7e45bed5de684e00632__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>4.1 supporting mistreatment of individual women – Expressing support for mistreatment of women as individuals. Support can be shown by denying, understating, or seeking to justify such mistreatment.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Media representations frame online cyber violence against women as gender-neutral and as an individual problem caused by women’s naivety or responsibility, advising women not to “feed the troll,” change privacy settings, or go offline. Such advice normalizes abuse, silences victims, and shifts blame to women by discouraging them from challenging sexist, racist, or misogynist language and attitudes. Media under-reporting and normalization of trolling events such as rape threats, death threats, and body shaming, alongside prevalent internet rape culture and anti-female violent expression, understate and implicitly justify mistreatment of individual women.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "answer_relevance_card_6a51d7e45bed5de684e00632__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
